bians, and fish). The biology, husbandry, diseases, pathology, and main research uses of these species will be covered. The course will meet for two hours weekly and will extend over the course of two years.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: basic knowledge of anatomy and pathology in comparative animal species.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: upper-level undergraduate\u00a0or graduate students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "VM", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2755, "crseId": 361233, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "VTBMS", "catalogNbr": "7130", "titleShort": "Cell Cycle Analysis", "titleLong": "Cell Cycle Analysis", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 14390, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "01/21/2020", "endDt": "05/05/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ay13", "firstName": "Andrew", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Yen"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/21/2020", "endDt": "05/12/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "HY", "instrModeDescrshort": "HY-OLIP", "instrModeDescr": "Hybrid - Online & In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "SUS", "gradingBasisShort": "Sat/Unsat", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "TOX", "catalogNbr": "7130", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/21/2020", "sessionEndDt": "05/12/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Presents a brief historical review of the cell cycle; a summary of cell-cycle regulatory processes; and practical methods for cell-cycle analysis, including mathematical representations. Topics include growth control of bacterial cell cycle including chemostats, mammalian-cell tissue culture, cell synchronization, flow cytometry, age-density representation, G1 regulation, labile regulatory protein models, cell transformation, regulation by growth factors and the cytoskeleton, cyclin/E2F/RB regulatory model, practical examples for analysis of cell-cycle phase durations, cell-cycle phase specific growth factor sensitivity, and timing of RB protein phosphorylation within the cell cycle. The objective of the course is to present graduate students with methods for cell-cycle analyses that will be used in their research.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring (offered alternate years).", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: 5 students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "VM", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2755, "crseId": 350911, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "VTBMS", "catalogNbr": "7200", "titleShort": "Biomedical Bio